/-!
# Global generation of a twist of the dualizing sheaf of a proper curve

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — let `ω` be the dualizing sheaf of `X` and let `ℒ` be an invertible
`𝒪_X`-module of degree at least two. [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] asserts that `ω ⊗ ℒ` is generated by its
global sections.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport` says that a
  module on `X` has no nonzero submodule whose support has dimension zero.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData` is the presentation of
  `ℱ` as an extension of a module with zero-dimensional support by `ω` that a section of `ℒ`
  vanishing at a point produces, together with the count of its global sections.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.epi_comp_cokernelπ_of_epi_comp`: for an exact `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` and a
  morphism `γ` into `ℱ` whose composite with `ℱ ⟶ 𝒬` is an epimorphism, the composite
  `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ coker(γ)` is an epimorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.supp_subset_of_mono` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_supp_le_of_supp_subset`: the support of a submodule is
  contained in the support of the ambient module, and its dimension is therefore no larger.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.subsingleton_modulesStalk_of_epi_of_range_le_maximalIdeal_smul`: **Nakayama
  at a point.** If `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒞` is epi and the image of `ω_x ⟶ ℱ_x` lies in `𝔪_x ℱ_x`, then
  `𝒞_x = 0`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData.two_le_finrank` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData.isZero_of_mono`: the two
  hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] that its source leaves unchecked.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData.epi_globalSections_quotient`
  and `...VanishingSectionData.subsingleton_modulesStalk_cokernel`: [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] at a
  vanishing section, and the Nakayama step it feeds.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.epi_globalSectionsHom_of_forall_isClosed`: the
  global sections of `ℱ` generate `ℱ`, from the data of a vanishing section at every closed
  point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.nonempty_generatingSections_tensorSheaf`:
  [Stacks, Tag 0B5H].

## Implementation notes

Global generation is the existence of a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, and the family used
is the family of *all* global sections, so global generation is exactly surjectivity of
`AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom`. Its cokernel `𝒞` is the obstruction, and the proof shows
`𝒞 = 0` by showing that `𝒞` vanishes at every closed point: `𝒞` is of finite type, so its
support is closed, and a nonempty closed subset of the proper scheme `X` contains a point closed
in `X`.

At a closed point `x` the source chooses, by [Stacks, Tag 0B58], a global section `s` of `ℒ`
vanishing at `x` but at no generic point of `X`, so that `𝒬 = coker(ω ⟶ ω ⊗ ℒ)` has
zero-dimensional support. [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] then makes the global sections of `ω ⊗ ℒ` surject
onto `𝒬`, which says exactly that `ω` surjects onto `𝒞`; since `s` vanishes at `x` the image of
`ω_x` lies in `𝔪_x (ω ⊗ ℒ)_x`, so `𝒞_x = 𝔪_x 𝒞_x` and Nakayama gives `𝒞_x = 0`.

**The two hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] which its source does not check are proved here.**
The lower bound `dim_k H⁰(X, 𝒬) ≥ 2` comes from the count of global sections of `𝒬` recorded in
`VanishingSectionData` together with `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2`. That no nonzero submodule of `ω ⊗ ℒ` injects
into `𝒬` follows from the zero-dimensionality of the support of `𝒬`: such a submodule has
zero-dimensional support as well, and `ω ⊗ ℒ` has no nonzero submodule supported in dimension
zero because `ω` is Cohen--Macaulay of dimension one.

**Hypotheses are carried for the external results this development lacks**, none of them an
assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H].

*The dualizing sheaf and duality.* There is no dualizing sheaf of a proper curve over a field in
this library, so `ω` is an unconstrained module and clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] is the
argument `hdual` while `dim_k H¹(X, ω) = 1` of Section [Stacks, Tag 0B5B] is `hone`. These are
the two inputs of [Stacks, Tag 0B5E] that
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.epi_globalSectionsHom_comp` also asks for. Its
third input, the vanishing of `H²(X, -)` of [Stacks, Tag 02UZ], is proved in this development as
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.secondCohomologyVanishing`, so the argument `hH2`
below is redundant; it is kept because [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] is stated with it.

*Cohen--Macaulayness of `ω`.* That `ω ⊗ ℒ` has no nonzero submodule supported in dimension zero
is `hnosub`, a statement about `ω ⊗ ℒ` alone.

*The vanishing section and the section count.* `VanishingSectionData` packages what
[Stacks, Tag 0B58] produces at a closed point, which is not in this library beyond the
projective-space case, together with the count `dim_k H⁰(X, 𝒬) = deg(ℒ)` of Section
[Stacks, Tag 0B5B]. Because [Stacks, Tag 0B58] needs `k` infinite and `x` a `k`-rational point,
the data is available for `k` algebraically closed; the reduction of the general case to that one
by base change is not carried out.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B58](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B58)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BS2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.ModuleSkyscraper (modulesStalkFunctor)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The cokernel of a morphism into an extension -/

/-- **The subobject generated by `γ` and by the image of `ω` is everything, if the image of `γ`
already surjects onto the quotient by `ω`.** Precisely: for an exact `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` in an
abelian category and a morphism `γ` into `ℱ` whose composite with `ℱ ⟶ 𝒬` is an epimorphism, the
composite `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ coker(γ)` is an epimorphism.

A morphism out of `coker(γ)` killing `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ coker(γ)` pulls back to a morphism out of `ℱ`
killing `ω`, which therefore descends along `ℱ ⟶ 𝒬`; the descent is killed by `γ ≫ β`, hence is
zero because that is an epimorphism; so the original morphism is killed by the epimorphism
`ℱ ⟶ coker(γ)` and is zero. -/
public theorem epi_comp_cokernelπ_of_epi_comp {A : Type*} [Category* A] [Abelian A]
    {W F Q G : A} (α : W ⟶ F) (β : F ⟶ Q) (hαβ : α ≫ β = 0)
    (hex : (ShortComplex.mk α β hαβ).Exact) [Epi β] (γ : G ⟶ F) (hγ : Epi (γ ≫ β)) :
    Epi (α ≫ cokernel.π γ) := by
  rw [Preadditive.epi_iff_cancel_zero]
  intro Z w hw
  have hv : α ≫ (cokernel.π γ ≫ w) = 0 := by rw [← Category.assoc]; exact hw
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := hex.desc' (cokernel.π γ ≫ w) hv
  have h0 : (γ ≫ β) ≫ l = 0 := by
    rw [Category.assoc, hl, ← Category.assoc, cokernel.condition, zero_comp]
  have hl0 : l = 0 := (Preadditive.epi_iff_cancel_zero _).mp hγ _ l h0
  have hπw : cokernel.π γ ≫ w = 0 := by rw [← hl, hl0, comp_zero]
  exact (Preadditive.epi_iff_cancel_zero _).mp inferInstance _ w hπw

/-! ### Supports of submodules, and finite type quotients -/

private alias supp_subset_of_mono_aux := AlgebraicGeometry.supp_subset_of_mono_stalkwise

/-- **The support of a submodule is contained in the support of the ambient module.** A
monomorphism of sheaves of modules is injective on every stalk, so a nonzero germ has nonzero
image. -/
public theorem supp_subset_of_mono {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules} (v : M ⟶ N) [h : Mono v] :
    SheafOfModules.supp M ⊆ SheafOfModules.supp N :=
  supp_subset_of_mono_aux (O := X.ringCatSheaf) v ⟨fun g₁ g₂ hg => h.right_cancellation g₁ g₂ hg⟩

/-- An inclusion of supports does not raise the dimension. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_supp_le_of_supp_subset {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules}
    (h : SheafOfModules.supp M ⊆ SheafOfModules.supp N) :
    topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp M) ≤ topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp N) :=
  (Topology.IsEmbedding.inclusion h).isInducing.topologicalKrullDim_le

private theorem isFiniteType_of_epi_aux {Y : TopCat.{u}}
    {O : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y) RingCat.{u}} {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} O}
    (p : M ⟶ N) (hp : Epi p) (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType :=
  have := hp
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi.{u, u, u} p hM

/-- **A quotient of a module of finite type is of finite type.** -/
private theorem isFiniteType_of_epi {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules} (p : M ⟶ N) [h : Epi p]
    (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType :=
  isFiniteType_of_epi_aux (O := X.ringCatSheaf) p
    ⟨fun g₁ g₂ hg => h.left_cancellation g₁ g₂ hg⟩ hM

private theorem isClosed_supp_aux {Y : TopCat.{u}}
    {O : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y) RingCat.{u}} (M : SheafOfModules.{u} O)
    (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : IsClosed (SheafOfModules.supp M) :=
  have := hM
  SheafOfModules.isClosed_supp M

/-- **The support of a module of finite type is closed.** -/
private theorem isClosed_supp {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) (hM : M.IsFiniteType) :
    IsClosed (SheafOfModules.supp M) :=
  isClosed_supp_aux (O := X.ringCatSheaf) M hM

/-! ### Nakayama at a point -/

/-- **Nakayama at a point.** If `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒞` is an epimorphism with `𝒞` of finite type, and the
image of `ω_x ⟶ ℱ_x` lies in `𝔪_x ℱ_x`, then the stalk `𝒞_x` vanishes.

The stalk functor at `x` is a left adjoint, so `ω_x ⟶ 𝒞_x` is onto; its image lies in
`𝔪_x 𝒞_x` because the image of `ω_x` in `ℱ_x` lies in `𝔪_x ℱ_x`. So `𝒞_x = 𝔪_x 𝒞_x`, and `𝒞_x`
is a finite module over the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}`, whose maximal ideal is its Jacobson radical. -/
public theorem subsingleton_modulesStalk_of_epi_of_range_le_maximalIdeal_smul
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (x : X) {W F C : X.Modules} (α : W ⟶ F) (π : F ⟶ C)
    (hC : C.IsFiniteType) (hepi : Epi (α ≫ π))
    (hv : LinearMap.range ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map α).hom ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).obj F))) :
    Subsingleton ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).obj C) := by
  have := hepi
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map (α ≫ π)).hom :=
    (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).mp inferInstance
  have := hC
  have hfin : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).obj C) :=
    SheafOfModules.finite_stalk X.sheaf C x
  have htop : (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).obj C)) ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) • ⊤ := by
    intro c _
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hsurj c
    have hmem : ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map α).hom w ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).obj F)) :=
      hv ⟨w, rfl⟩
    have himg := Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (f := ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map π).hom) hmem
    rw [Submodule.map_smul''] at himg
    have hle : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) •
        Submodule.map ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map π).hom ⊤ ≤
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) • ⊤ :=
      Submodule.smul_le.mpr fun r hr n _ => Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr Submodule.mem_top
    have hcomp : ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map (α ≫ π)).hom w =
        ((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map π).hom (((modulesStalkFunctor X x).map α).hom w) := by
      rw [Functor.map_comp]; rfl
    rw [← hw, hcomp]
    exact hle himg
  have hbot := Submodule.eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ⊤ hfin.fg_top htop
    (by rw [IsLocalRing.jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal ⊥ bot_ne_top])
  exact subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun a => (Submodule.eq_bot_iff _).mp hbot a trivial

/-! ### Global generation as surjectivity of the map from the free module on all sections -/

/-- **A module whose global sections span it is generated by global sections**, the family of
generators being the family of all global sections. -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_of_epi_globalSectionsHom {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (F : X.Modules) (h : Epi (globalSectionsHom F)) : Nonempty F.GeneratingSections :=
  ⟨⟨F.sections, id, h⟩⟩

namespace CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

variable (S : CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.{u})

/-! ### The two carried geometric inputs -/

/-- **A module with no nonzero submodule supported in dimension zero.** For `ω ⊗ ℒ` with `ω` the
dualizing sheaf of `X` this holds because `ω` is Cohen--Macaulay of dimension one. -/
public def NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport (F : S.X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∀ (M : S.X.Modules) (u : M ⟶ F), Mono u →
    topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp M) ≤ 0 → IsZero M

/-- **The presentation of `ℱ` produced by a section of `ℒ` vanishing at `x`**, as
[Stacks, Tag 0B58] provides it at a closed `k`-rational point of a curve over an infinite field:
an exact sequence `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` whose quotient `𝒬` is quasi-coherent with zero-dimensional
support and has `d` global sections, and whose first map has image inside `𝔪_x ℱ_x` at `x`. For
`ℱ = ω ⊗ ℒ` the count `d` is the degree of `ℒ`. -/
public structure VanishingSectionData (ω F : S.X.Modules) (d : ℤ) (x : S.X) where
  /-- The quotient of `ℱ` by the image of `ω`. -/
  Q : S.X.Modules
  /-- Multiplication by the chosen section of `ℒ`. -/
  α : ω ⟶ F
  /-- The quotient map. -/
  β : F ⟶ Q
  /-- The two maps compose to zero. -/
  comp_eq_zero : α ≫ β = 0
  /-- The sequence `ω ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒬` is exact at `ℱ`. -/
  exact : (ShortComplex.mk α β comp_eq_zero).Exact
  /-- `𝒬` is a quotient of `ℱ`. -/
  epi : Epi β
  /-- `𝒬` is quasi-coherent. -/
  isQuasicoherent : Q.IsQuasicoherent
  /-- The support of `𝒬` has dimension zero. -/
  supp_dim_le : topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp Q) ≤ 0
  /-- `H¹(X, -)` vanishes on every submodule of `𝒬`. -/
  firstCohomologyVanishingOnSub : S.FirstCohomologyVanishingOnSub Q
  /-- A quotient of `𝒬` with no global sections is zero. -/
  isZeroOnQuotientsWithoutSections : S.IsZeroOnQuotientsWithoutSections Q
  /-- `𝒬` has `d` global sections. -/
  finrank_cohomology_zero : (Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f Q 0) : ℤ) = d
  /-- The chosen section vanishes at `x`. -/
  range_modulesStalk_le :
    LinearMap.range ((modulesStalkFunctor S.X x).map α).hom ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) ((modulesStalkFunctor S.X x).obj F))

variable {S}

/-! ### The two hypotheses of Stacks Tag 0B5F -/

/-- **`dim_k H⁰(X, 𝒬) ≥ 2`**, the first hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0B5F]: the quotient has `d`
global sections, and `d` is at least two. -/
public theorem VanishingSectionData.two_le_finrank {ω F : S.X.Modules} {d : ℤ} {x : S.X}
    (D : S.VanishingSectionData ω F d x) (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    2 ≤ Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f D.Q 0) := by
  have h := D.finrank_cohomology_zero
  omega

/-- **No nonzero submodule of `ℱ` injects into `𝒬`**, the second hypothesis of
[Stacks, Tag 0B5F]: a submodule of `ℱ` injecting into `𝒬` has support inside the support of
`𝒬`, hence of dimension zero, and `ℱ` has no nonzero submodule supported in dimension zero. -/
public theorem VanishingSectionData.isZero_of_mono {ω F : S.X.Modules} {d : ℤ} {x : S.X}
    (D : S.VanishingSectionData ω F d x) (hnosub : S.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport F)
    (M : S.X.Modules) (u : M ⟶ F) (hu : Mono u) (huβ : Mono (u ≫ D.β)) : IsZero M :=
  have := huβ
  hnosub M u hu ((topologicalKrullDim_supp_le_of_supp_subset
    (supp_subset_of_mono (u ≫ D.β))).trans D.supp_dim_le)

/-! ### Global generation -/

/-- **The global sections of `ℱ` generate it modulo the image of `ω`**, by [Stacks, Tag 0B5F]
applied to the presentation of `ℱ` attached to a vanishing section.

[Stacks, Tag 0B5F] reads the zero-dimensional support of `𝒬` itself, so the field
`supp_dim_le` of the vanishing section data is what is passed to it, and coherence of `ℱ` —
quasi-coherence together with `hFft` on the locally Noetherian `X` — is what it needs of `ℱ`.
It proves the vanishing of `H²(X, -)` rather than consuming it, so `_hH2` is unused here; it is
retained so that the three results below keep the statements they have. -/
public theorem VanishingSectionData.epi_globalSections_quotient {ω F : S.X.Modules} {d : ℤ}
    {x : S.X} (D : S.VanishingSectionData ω F d x) (hωq : ω.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherent) (hFft : F.IsFiniteType) (hdual : S.FirstCohomologyDuality ω)
    (_hH2 : S.SecondCohomologyVanishing)
    (hone : Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f ω 1) = 1)
    (hnosub : S.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport F) (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    Epi (globalSectionsHom F ≫ D.β) :=
  have := D.epi
  epi_globalSectionsHom_comp hωq hFq hFft D.isQuasicoherent hdual hone D.α D.β D.comp_eq_zero
    D.exact D.supp_dim_le (D.two_le_finrank hd) (D.isZero_of_mono hnosub)

/-- **The cokernel of the map from the free module on all global sections of `ℱ` vanishes at
`x`.** The global sections of `ℱ` generate it modulo the image of `ω`, so `ω` surjects onto that
cokernel; the chosen section vanishes at `x`, so the image of `ω_x` lies in `𝔪_x ℱ_x`; Nakayama
finishes. -/
public theorem VanishingSectionData.subsingleton_modulesStalk_cokernel {ω F : S.X.Modules}
    {d : ℤ} {x : S.X} (D : S.VanishingSectionData ω F d x) (hωq : ω.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherent) (hFft : F.IsFiniteType) (hdual : S.FirstCohomologyDuality ω)
    (hH2 : S.SecondCohomologyVanishing)
    (hone : Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f ω 1) = 1)
    (hnosub : S.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport F) (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    Subsingleton ((modulesStalkFunctor S.X x).obj (cokernel (globalSectionsHom F))) :=
  have := D.epi
  subsingleton_modulesStalk_of_epi_of_range_le_maximalIdeal_smul x D.α
    (cokernel.π (globalSectionsHom F))
    (isFiniteType_of_epi (cokernel.π (globalSectionsHom F)) hFft)
    (epi_comp_cokernelπ_of_epi_comp D.α D.β D.comp_eq_zero D.exact (globalSectionsHom F)
      (D.epi_globalSections_quotient hωq hFq hFft hdual hH2 hone hnosub hd))
    D.range_modulesStalk_le

/-- **The global sections of `ℱ` generate `ℱ`**, given at every closed point of `X` a section of
`ℒ` vanishing there in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.VanishingSectionData`.

The cokernel `𝒞` of the map from the free module on all global sections of `ℱ` is of finite
type, so its support is closed; were it nonempty it would contain a point closed in the proper
scheme `X`, and at such a point `𝒞` vanishes. -/
public theorem epi_globalSectionsHom_of_forall_isClosed {ω F : S.X.Modules}
    (hωq : ω.IsQuasicoherent) (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherent) (hFft : F.IsFiniteType)
    (hdual : S.FirstCohomologyDuality ω) (hH2 : S.SecondCohomologyVanishing)
    (hone : Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f ω 1) = 1)
    (hnosub : S.NoSubmoduleOfZeroDimensionalSupport F) {d : ℤ} (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hsec : ∀ x : S.X, IsClosed ({x} : Set S.X) → S.VanishingSectionData ω F d x) :
    Epi (globalSectionsHom F) := by
  have : CompactSpace S.X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace S.f
  refine epi_of_isZero_cokernel _ ?_
  refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.DevissageNoetherian.isZero_of_supp_eq_empty _ ?_
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hxcl⟩ := Stacks.SerreAffinenessCriterion.exists_isClosed_singleton_mem
    (isClosed_supp (cokernel (globalSectionsHom F))
      (isFiniteType_of_epi (cokernel.π (globalSectionsHom F)) hFft))
    (Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.mpr hne)
